Q(2)
| **for Loop**                                                                     | **while Loop**                                                                                 |
| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Used when the number of iterations is known.                                     | Used when the number of iterations is not known.                                               |
| Initialization, condition, and increment/decrement are written in one statement. | Initialization is written before the loop, and increment/decrement is written inside the loop. |
| Easier to read for counting loops.                                               | Better for condition-based loops.                                                              |
| Syntax: `for(initialization; condition; increment)`                              | Syntax: `while(condition)`


|
